scenario a position relayed by a node can be stale on arrival
describe The second route to Stale, and the one that has nothing to do with a
describe receiver going quiet: an observation that was already old when it got
describe here. An Attadipa node carries the GNSS for a watch that has none, and
describe the position crosses a link that can queue, retry and reconnect.
describe
describe `age` is the fixture's way of saying the observation's own timestamp
describe is older than the moment it is being judged at — which is exactly what
describe the wire gives us, because observed_at travels with the observation
describe and is not the time of arrival.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3000
  sats 11 14
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted

# Two seconds in flight. Well inside the window; nothing to say about it.
at 10000
  fix 3d
  age 2000
  pos 5000180 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3000
  sats 11 14
  expect validity valid
  expect no-reason stale-position

# The link stalled and delivered a backlog. This one was taken forty seconds
# ago, and the fact that it arrived a moment ago does not make it current.
at 60000
  fix 3d
  age 40000
  pos 5000400 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3000
  sats 11 14
  expect validity stale
  expect reason stale-position

# Fresh again the moment a current one arrives. Staleness is a property of the
# observation, not a mood the device gets into.
at 61000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000420 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3000
  sats 11 14
  expect validity valid
  expect no-reason stale-position
